PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L07U4.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":7,"cefr":"B1+","unit":4,"theme":"Choices and Consequences","essential_question":"How do our choices shape our lives?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS1","title":"If I Had Gone to Bed Early…: The Third Conditional","objectives":["Students will be able to use the third conditional to talk about how the past could have been different.","Students will be able to use would have, could have and might have in the result clause.","I can say \"If I had gone to bed early, I would have woken up on time.\"","I can talk about past choices and their results."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام الشرط الثالث للتحدث عن كيف كان يمكن أن يكون الماضي مختلفًا.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام would have وcould have وmight have في جواب الشرط.","أستطيع أن أقول If I had gone to bed early, I would have woken up on time.","أستطيع أن أتحدث عن خيارات الماضي ونتائجها."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"consequence","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɑnsəkwəns/","definition":"a result of an action, often a bad one","arabic":"عاقبة / نتيجة","example":"Every choice has consequences.","image_id":"GV-L07-U4-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS1-W01"},{"word":"regret","pos":"verb","ipa":"/rəˈɡrɛt/","definition":"to feel sorry about something you did or didn't do","arabic":"يندم على","example":"I regret not saying goodbye to my teacher.","image_id":"GV-L07-U4-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS1-W02"},{"word":"decision","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dɪˈsɪʒən/","definition":"a choice you make after thinking","arabic":"قرار","example":"Choosing a university is a big decision.","image_id":"GV-L07-U4-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS1-W03"},{"word":"choice","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tʃɔɪs/","definition":"the act of choosing, or something you choose","arabic":"اختيار","example":"You made a wise choice.","image_id":"GV-L07-U4-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"The third conditional talks about an imaginary past – something that did not happen and its imaginary result: If I had gone to bed early, I would have woken up on time. (In reality, I went to bed late and woke up late.)\nForm: If + past perfect (had + past participle), would have + past participle. Use could have for ability or possibility and might have when you aren't sure: If I had been more careful, I might have gotten a better grade.\nPut a comma after the if-clause when it comes first. No comma when if comes second: I would have woken up on time if I had gone to bed early. Never use would in the if-clause: (not: If I would have known…) → If I had known…\nIf + had + past participle, would have + past participle\ncould have (ability) • might have (possibility)\nno would in the if-clause • comma after the if-clause when it is first\nmeaning: the opposite of what really happened","examples":["If Adam had set an alarm, he wouldn't have overslept.","If it hadn't rained, we would have played outside.","She would have won the race if she hadn't fallen.","If you had told me, I could have helped you.","If we had taken the other road, we might have arrived earlier.","If Faisal hadn't worn a helmet, he would have been badly hurt.","What would you have said if the principal had asked you?","If I hadn't joined the club, I wouldn't have met my best friend."],"common_errors":["✗ If I would have known, I would have come. → ✓ If I had known, I would have come. (No would in the if-clause.)","✗ If I had studied, I would passed. → ✓ If I had studied, I would have passed. (would + have + past participle.)","✗ If she had went to the doctor, she would have felt better. → ✓ If she had gone to the doctor, … (had + past participle (gone).)","✗ If I hadn't missed the bus I wouldn't have been late. → ✓ If I hadn't missed the bus, I wouldn't have been late. (Comma after the if-clause.)"],"arabic":"الشرط الثالث يتحدث عن ماضٍ متخيَّل لم يحدث ونتيجته المتخيَّلة: If I had gone to bed early, I would have woken up on time (لو نمتُ مبكرًا لاستيقظتُ في الوقت).\nالتركيب: If + had + التصريف الثالث، would have + التصريف الثالث.\ncould have للقدرة وmight have للاحتمال.\nلا نستخدم would بعد if، ونضع فاصلة بعد جملة الشرط إذا جاءت أولًا."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “If I Had Gone to Bed Early…: The Third Conditional”. Let’s learn third conditional (if + past perfect, would have + past participle) for imaginary past situations; could have / might have; negatives; comma rules together.","on_screen":"GV-L07-U4-LS1 | If I Had Gone to Bed Early…: The Third Conditional","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “The Night I Made the Wrong Choice”: Last May, I made a choice that taught me an important lesson. It was the night before our final math exam, and my friends invited me to join an online game. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Last May, I made a choice that taught me an important lesson. It was the night before our final math exam, and my friends invited me to join an online game.","visual":"Image GV-L07-U4-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"The third conditional talks about an imaginary past – something that did not happen and its imaginary result: If I had gone to bed early, I would have woken up on time. (In reality, I went to bed late and woke up late.) Form: If + past perfect (had + past participle), would have + past participle. Use could have for ability or possibility and might have when you aren't sure: If I had been more careful, I might have gotten a better grade.","on_screen":"If + had + past participle, would have + past participle • could have (ability) • might have (possibility) • no would in the if-clause • comma after the if-clause when it is first","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. If Adam had set an alarm, he wouldn't have overslept. If it hadn't rained, we would have played outside. She would have won the race if she hadn't fallen.","on_screen":"If Adam had set an alarm, he wouldn't have overslept. / If it hadn't rained, we would have played outside. / She would have won the race if she hadn't fallen.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “If I would have known, I would have come.” That’s not right. We say: “If I had known, I would have come.” No would in the if-clause.","on_screen":"✗ If I would have known, I would have come.   ✓ If I had known, I would have come.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"If I had gone to bed early, I would have woken up on time.\" Did I go to bed early? … Think! … No. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"If I had gone to bed early, I would have woken up on time.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"If I had gone to bed early, I would have woken up on time.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: third conditional (if + past perfect, would have + past participle) for imaginary past situations; could have / might have; negatives; comma rules.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الشرط الثالث يتحدث عن ماضٍ متخيَّل لم يحدث ونتيجته المتخيَّلة: If I had gone to bed early, I would have woken up on time (لو نمتُ مبكرًا لاستيقظتُ في الوقت).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: If I would have known, I would have come. — الصحيح: If I had known, I would have come.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول If I had gone to bed early, I would have woken up on time."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"The Night I Made the Wrong Choice","body":"Last May, I made a choice that taught me an important lesson. It was the night before our final math exam, and my friends invited me to join an online game. \"Just one hour,\" I told myself. But one hour became four, and I went to bed at two in the morning.\nThe next day, I woke up late and missed the school bus. My father had to drive me, and I arrived just as the exam started. I was so tired that I couldn't concentrate, and I made silly mistakes in questions I knew well. I got 61 out of 100.\nWhen I saw my result, I felt terrible. If I had gone to bed early, I would have woken up on time. If I hadn't missed the bus, my father wouldn't have been late for work. And if I had been more careful, I might have gotten a much better grade.\nMy father didn't shout at me. He said that everyone makes mistakes, but the smart thing is to learn from them. He was right. If he had been angry, I probably wouldn't have listened.\nThis year, I've made a new rule: no games on school nights. I faced the consequences of a bad decision, and I'm not going to make the same mistake again.","word_count":217,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"If I had gone to bed early, I ___ up on time.","options":["will have woken","would have woken","would wake","had woken"],"answer":"would have woken","explanation":"result → would have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الجواب ← would have."},{"q":"If Saad ___ the bus, his father wouldn't have been late for work.","options":["hasn't missed","wouldn't have missed","hadn't missed","didn't miss"],"answer":"hadn't missed","explanation":"if-clause → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط ← had + التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"If we had left home earlier, we ___ the beginning of the match.","options":["didn't miss","hadn't missed","won't miss","wouldn't have missed"],"answer":"wouldn't have missed","explanation":"Negatives: hadn't / wouldn't have.","explanation_ar":"النفي."},{"q":"If you had asked me, I ___ have helped you – I'm not sure.","options":["will","had","did","might"],"answer":"might","explanation":"could have / might have.","explanation_ar":"could have وmight have."},{"q":"","options":["If I had known about the test, I would have studied.","If I knew about the test, I would studied.","If I had knew about the test, I would have studied.","If I would have known about the test, I would have studied."],"answer":"If I had known about the test, I would have studied.","explanation":"Comma after the if-clause when it comes first; no would after if.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة ولا would بعد if."},{"q":"\"If Lina had trained more, she would have won the race.\" Did Lina win the race?","options":["No, she didn't.","She trained a lot.","Yes, she did.","She will win it next week."],"answer":"No, she didn't.","explanation":"The third conditional means the opposite of what happened.","explanation_ar":"المعنى عكس ما حدث."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the correct form. Word bank: had saved, would have played, wouldn't have gotten","items":[{"q":"If it hadn't rained, we ______ (play) football outside.","options":[],"answer":"would have played","explanation":"result → would have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الجواب ← would have."},{"q":"If Omar ______ (save) his work, he wouldn't have lost his essay.","options":[],"answer":"had saved","explanation":"if-clause → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط ← had + التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"If they had checked the map, they ______ (not / get) lost.","options":[],"answer":"wouldn't have gotten","explanation":"Negatives: hadn't / wouldn't have.","explanation_ar":"النفي."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Write third conditional sentences about what really happened.","items":[{"q":"I didn't set an alarm, so I woke up late.  (third conditional)","options":[],"answer":"If I had set an alarm, I wouldn't have woken up late.","explanation":"if-clause → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط ← had + التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"Faisal forgot his passport, so he missed the flight.  (third conditional)","options":[],"answer":"If Faisal hadn't forgotten his passport, he wouldn't have missed the flight.","explanation":"Negatives: hadn't / wouldn't have.","explanation_ar":"النفي."},{"q":"We took a taxi, so we arrived on time.  (third conditional)","options":[],"answer":"If we hadn't taken a taxi, we wouldn't have arrived on time.","explanation":"result → would have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الجواب ← would have."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Imagine a different past.","items":[{"q":"If I had been born in another country, I would have ___.","options":[],"answer":"If I had been born in Japan, I would have learned Japanese.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses third conditional (if + past perfect, would have + past participle) for imaginary past situations; could have / might have; negatives; comma rules correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"If I hadn't come to this school, I wouldn't have ___.","options":[],"answer":"If I hadn't come to this school, I wouldn't have met my best friend.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses third conditional (if + past perfect, would have + past participle) for imaginary past situations; could have / might have; negatives; comma rules correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A small choice that changed your day: If I had ___, I would have ___.","options":[],"answer":"If I had brought my lunch, I wouldn't have been hungry all afternoon.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses third conditional (if + past perfect, would have + past participle) for imaginary past situations; could have / might have; negatives; comma rules correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with could have.","options":[],"answer":"If I had practiced more, I could have played in the final.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses third conditional (if + past perfect, would have + past participle) for imaginary past situations; could have / might have; negatives; comma rules correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with might have.","options":[],"answer":"If we had asked the teacher, she might have given us more time.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses third conditional (if + past perfect, would have + past participle) for imaginary past situations; could have / might have; negatives; comma rules correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: A chain of consequences.","items":[{"q":"Write a true sentence about something that went wrong.","options":[],"answer":"I forgot to charge my phone last Thursday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses third conditional (if + past perfect, would have + past participle) for imaginary past situations; could have / might have; negatives; comma rules correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a chain of 3 third conditional sentences about it.","options":[],"answer":"If I had charged my phone, I would have seen my mom's message. If I had seen her message, I would have gone to the right gate. If I had gone to the right gate, I wouldn't have waited for an hour.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses third conditional (if + past perfect, would have + past participle) for imaginary past situations; could have / might have; negatives; comma rules correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask a partner one \"What would you have done if…?\" question and write his answer.","options":[],"answer":"What would you have done if you had lost your wallet? – He said he would have gone to the police station.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses third conditional (if + past perfect, would have + past participle) for imaginary past situations; could have / might have; negatives; comma rules correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Four Corners Grammar","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a sentence frame with a cue word and four possible answers (A–D).","Students walk to the corner with the correct answer.","One student in each corner explains the choice in one sentence.","Correct corner scores a point; continue with the next cue."],"data":[{"label":"If I had…, I would have…"},{"label":"If she hadn't…, she wouldn't have…"},{"label":"I wish I had…"},{"label":"If only I hadn't…"},{"label":"I should have…"},{"label":"might have…"},{"label":"could have…"},{"label":"make a choice"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"If Lina had brought her calculator, she ___ the problems faster.","options":["would solve","had solved","would have solved","will solve"],"answer":"would have solved","explanation":"result → would have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الجواب ← would have."},{"q":"If I ___ that the shop was closed, I wouldn't have gone there.","options":["had known","would have known","have known","knew"],"answer":"had known","explanation":"if-clause → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط ← had + التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"","options":["If they wouldn't have helped us, we wouldn't have finished on time.","If they didn't help us, we wouldn't have finished on time.","If they hadn't helped us, we wouldn't have finished on time.","If they hadn't helped us, we didn't finish on time."],"answer":"If they hadn't helped us, we wouldn't have finished on time.","explanation":"Negatives: hadn't / wouldn't have.","explanation_ar":"النفي."},{"q":"If you had entered the competition, you ___ have won. Who knows?","options":["had","might","would to","will"],"answer":"might","explanation":"could have / might have.","explanation_ar":"could have وmight have."},{"q":"\"If the referee had seen the foul, he would have given a penalty.\" Did the referee see the foul?","options":["He saw it later.","We can't know anything.","No.","Yes."],"answer":"No.","explanation":"The third conditional means the opposite of what happened.","explanation_ar":"المعنى عكس ما حدث."},{"q":"","options":["We would have stayed longer if the hotel hadn't been so noisy.","We would stay longer if the hotel hadn't been so noisy.","We would have stayed longer if the hotel wouldn't have been so noisy.","We would have stayed longer, if the hotel hadn't been so noisy."],"answer":"We would have stayed longer if the hotel hadn't been so noisy.","explanation":"Comma after the if-clause when it comes first; no would after if.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة ولا would بعد if."},{"q":"If he had worn his seatbelt, he ___ hurt.","options":["wouldn't be","wouldn't have been","won't be","hadn't been"],"answer":"wouldn't have been","explanation":"Negatives: hadn't / wouldn't have.","explanation_ar":"النفي."},{"q":"What would you have done if your phone ___ during the exam?","options":["would have rung","had rung","has rung","rang"],"answer":"had rung","explanation":"if-clause → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط ← had + التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"If I had saved my money, I ___ have bought the new game.","options":["can","will","did","could"],"answer":"could","explanation":"could have / might have.","explanation_ar":"could have وmight have."},{"q":"","options":["If my brother hadn't called me, I would forget the meeting.","If my brother hadn't called me I would have forgotten the meeting.","If my brother wouldn't call me, I would have forgotten the meeting.","If my brother hadn't called me, I would have forgotten the meeting."],"answer":"If my brother hadn't called me, I would have forgotten the meeting.","explanation":"Comma after the if-clause when it comes first; no would after if.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة ولا would بعد if."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Split illustration: on the left, Saad gaming late at night with a clock showing 2:00 a.m.; on the right, Saad running late to an exam hall with his father's car behind him; a thought bubble shows an alternative scene of Saad sleeping at 10:00 p.m. and smiling at an exam paper marked 95. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Split illustration: on the left, Saad gaming late at night with a clock showing 2:00 a.m.; on the right, Saad running late to an exam hall with his father's car behind him; a thought bubble shows an alternative scene of Saad sleeping at 10:00 p.m. and smiling at an exam paper marked 95"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about third conditional (if + past perfect, would have + past participle) for imaginary past situations; could have / might have; negatives; comma rules, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about third conditional (if + past perfect, would have + past participle) for imaginary past situations"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows consequence (a result of an action, often a bad one); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing consequence: a result of an action, often a bad one"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows regret (to feel sorry about something you did or didn't do); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing regret: to feel sorry about something you did or didn't do"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows decision (a choice you make after thinking); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing decision: a choice you make after thinking"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows choice (the act of choosing, or something you choose); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing choice: the act of choosing, or something you choose"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Four Corners Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Four Corners Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS1-W01","script":"consequence. consequence. Every choice has consequences.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS1-W02","script":"regret. regret. I regret not saying goodbye to my teacher.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS1-W03","script":"decision. decision. Choosing a university is a big decision.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS1-W04","script":"choice. choice. You made a wise choice.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS1-T1","script":"Last May, I made a choice that taught me an important lesson. It was the night before our final math exam, and my friends invited me to join an online game. \"Just one hour,\" I told myself. But one hour became four, and I went to bed at two in the morning. The next day, I woke up late and missed the school bus. My father had to drive me, and I arrived just as the exam started. I was so tired that I couldn't concentrate, and I made silly mistakes in questions I knew well. I got 61 out of 100. When I saw my result, I felt terrible. If I had gone to bed early, I would have woken up on time. If I hadn't missed the bus, my father wouldn't have been late for work. And if I had been more careful, I might have gotten a much better grade. My father didn't shout at me. He said that everyone makes mistakes, but the smart thing is to learn from them. He was right. If he had been angry, I probably wouldn't have listened. This year, I've made a new rule: no games on school nights. I faced the consequences of a bad decision, and I'm not going to make the same mistake again.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “If I Had Gone to Bed Early…: The Third Conditional”. Let’s learn third conditional (if + past perfect, would have + past participle) for imaginary past situations; could have / might have; negatives; comma rules together. Listen to the start of “The Night I Made the Wrong Choice”: Last May, I made a choice that taught me an important lesson. It was the night before our final math exam, and my friends invited me to join an online game. Look at the green words. The third conditional talks about an imaginary past – something that did not happen and its imaginary result: If I had gone to bed early, I would have woken up on time. (In reality, I went to bed late and woke up late.) Form: If + past perfect (had + past participle), would have + past participle. Use could have for ability or possibility and might have when you aren't sure: If I had been more careful, I might have gotten a better grade. Here are some examples. If Adam had set an alarm, he wouldn't have overslept. If it hadn't rained, we would have played outside. She would have won the race if she hadn't fallen. Be careful! Some learners say: “If I would have known, I would have come.” That’s not right. We say: “If I had known, I would have come.” No would in the if-clause. Quick check: \"If I had gone to bed early, I would have woken up on time.\" Did I go to bed early? … Think! … No. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"If I had gone to bed early, I would have woken up on time.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS2","title":"I Wish I Had Listened: wish, if only and should have","objectives":["Students will be able to express regrets about the past with wish and if only + past perfect.","Students will be able to criticize past actions with should have / shouldn't have and tell past wishes from present wishes.","I can say \"I wish I had listened to my father.\"","I can say \"You shouldn't have shared your password.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من التعبير عن الندم على الماضي بـ wish وif only + الماضي التام.","سيتمكن الطلاب من انتقاد أفعال الماضي بـ should have / shouldn't have والتمييز بين أمنيات الماضي وأمنيات الحاضر.","أستطيع أن أقول I wish I had listened to my father.","أستطيع أن أقول You shouldn't have shared your password."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"option","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɑpʃən/","definition":"one of the things you can choose","arabic":"خيار / بديل","example":"We have three options for the trip.","image_id":"GV-L07-U4-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS2-W01"},{"word":"risk","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rɪsk/","definition":"the chance that something bad will happen","arabic":"مخاطرة","example":"Don't take risks when you swim in the sea.","image_id":"GV-L07-U4-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS2-W02"},{"word":"priority","pos":"noun","ipa":"/praɪˈɔrəti/","definition":"the thing that is most important to do first","arabic":"أولوية","example":"My priority this week is my science project.","image_id":"GV-L07-U4-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS2-W03"},{"word":"hesitate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈhɛzəˌteɪt/","definition":"to stop for a moment before you act because you aren't sure","arabic":"يتردّد","example":"Don't hesitate to ask for help.","image_id":"GV-L07-U4-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"To talk about regrets about the past, use wish + past perfect: I wish I had listened to my father. (I didn't listen, and now I'm sorry.) If only is stronger and more emotional: If only I hadn't missed the bus!\nCompare with a present wish: wish + past simple: I wish I had a laptop. (I don't have one now.) Past regret: I wish I had bought that laptop. (I didn't buy it.)\nUse should have / shouldn't have + past participle to criticize a past action or say what was the right thing to do: You should have told me. He shouldn't have shared his password. Don't use the past simple after should: (not: I should told).\nwish / if only + had + past participle (past regret)\nwish + past simple (present wish)\nshould have / shouldn't have + past participle (criticism, regret)\nNot: I wish I didn't eat so much yesterday. → I wish I hadn't eaten…","examples":["I wish I had brought an umbrella.","If only I hadn't eaten that third plate of kabsa!","My brother wishes he had studied engineering.","We should have left earlier.","You shouldn't have said that to your sister.","Lina wishes she hadn't hesitated before she answered.","I wish I lived closer to school. (present)","They should have considered all the options."],"common_errors":["✗ I wish I studied harder for yesterday's test. → ✓ I wish I had studied harder for yesterday's test. (Past regret → past perfect.)","✗ If only I didn't lose my keys yesterday! → ✓ If only I hadn't lost my keys yesterday! (Past → past perfect.)","✗ You should told me. → ✓ You should have told me. (should + have + past participle.)","✗ I wish I would have gone. → ✓ I wish I had gone. (After wish for the past → past perfect, not would have.)"],"arabic":"للندم على الماضي نستخدم wish + الماضي التام: I wish I had listened to my father (ليتني استمعت إلى أبي).\nif only أقوى في التعبير: If only I hadn't missed the bus!\nأمنية الحاضر بالماضي البسيط: I wish I had a laptop (ليت عندي حاسوبًا الآن).\nshould have / shouldn't have + التصريف الثالث للانتقاد: You should have told me (كان يجب أن تخبرني)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I Wish I Had Listened: wish, if only and should have”. Let’s learn wish / if only + past perfect for regrets about the past; contrast with wish + past simple for the present; should have / shouldn't have + past participle for criticism and regret together.","on_screen":"GV-L07-U4-LS2 | I Wish I Had Listened: wish, if only and should have","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: I wish I had saved my work. If only we hadn't left so late! Do you wish you had chosen a different subject?","on_screen":"I wish I had saved my work. | If only we hadn't left so late! | Do you wish you had chosen a different subject?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"To talk about regrets about the past, use wish + past perfect: I wish I had listened to my father. (I didn't listen, and now I'm sorry.) If only is stronger and more emotional: If only I hadn't missed the bus! Compare with a present wish: wish + past simple: I wish I had a laptop. (I don't have one now.) Past regret: I wish I had bought that laptop. (I didn't buy it.)","on_screen":"wish / if only + had + past participle (past regret) • wish + past simple (present wish) • should have / shouldn't have + past participle (criticism, regret)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I wish I had brought an umbrella. If only I hadn't eaten that third plate of kabsa! My brother wishes he had studied engineering.","on_screen":"I wish I had brought an umbrella. / If only I hadn't eaten that third plate of kabsa! / My brother wishes he had studied engineering.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I wish I studied harder for yesterday's test.” That’s not right. We say: “I wish I had studied harder for yesterday's test.” Past regret → past perfect.","on_screen":"✗ I wish I studied harder for yesterday's test.   ✓ I wish I had studied harder for yesterday's test.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"I wish I had listened to my father.\" Did I listen? … Think! … No. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I wish I had listened to my father.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"I wish I had listened to my father.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: wish / if only + past perfect for regrets about the past; contrast with wish + past simple for the present; should have / shouldn't have + past participle for criticism and regret.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","للندم على الماضي نستخدم wish + الماضي التام: I wish I had listened to my father (ليتني استمعت إلى أبي).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I wish I studied harder for yesterday's test. — الصحيح: I wish I had studied harder for yesterday's test.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول I wish I had listened to my father."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"I failed the test. I wish I ___ harder.","options":["have studied","would study","had studied","studied"],"answer":"had studied","explanation":"wish + had + past participle for past regrets.","explanation_ar":"wish للندم على الماضي."},{"q":"If only we ___ so much junk food last night!","options":["wouldn't eat","didn't eat","haven't eaten","hadn't eaten"],"answer":"hadn't eaten","explanation":"if only + had + past participle (strong regret).","explanation_ar":"if only."},{"q":"I don't have a bike. I wish I ___ one.","options":["had","have","had had","would have had"],"answer":"had","explanation":"wish + past simple for a present wish.","explanation_ar":"أمنية الحاضر."},{"q":"You ___ told me earlier! Now it's too late.","options":["shouldn't have","should have","would","should"],"answer":"should have","explanation":"should have / shouldn't have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"should have."},{"q":"","options":["She wishes she didn't shout at her brother yesterday.","She wishes she hadn't shouted at her brother.","She wishes she hasn't shouted at her brother.","She wishes she wouldn't shouted at her brother."],"answer":"She wishes she hadn't shouted at her brother.","explanation":"wish + had + past participle for past regrets.","explanation_ar":"wish للندم على الماضي."},{"q":"Which sentence is a regret about the past?","options":["I wish I had a warmer jacket.","I wish it would stop raining.","I wish I had brought my jacket.","I want a new jacket."],"answer":"I wish I had brought my jacket.","explanation":"Past regret or present wish?","explanation_ar":"الماضي أم الحاضر؟"}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the correct form. Word bank: hadn't told, shouldn't have laughed, had brought","items":[{"q":"I left my umbrella at home. I wish I ______ (bring) it.","options":[],"answer":"had brought","explanation":"wish + had + past participle for past regrets.","explanation_ar":"wish للندم على الماضي."},{"q":"If only Adam ______ (not / tell) everyone my secret!","options":[],"answer":"hadn't told","explanation":"if only + had + past participle (strong regret).","explanation_ar":"if only."},{"q":"We were rude to the new student. We ______ (not / laugh) at him.","options":[],"answer":"shouldn't have laughed","explanation":"should have / shouldn't have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"should have."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Write wishes and regrets.","items":[{"q":"I didn't apologize to my friend. (wish)","options":[],"answer":"I wish I had apologized to my friend.","explanation":"wish + had + past participle for past regrets.","explanation_ar":"wish للندم على الماضي."},{"q":"We spent all our money on the first day of the trip. (If only)","options":[],"answer":"If only we hadn't spent all our money on the first day of the trip!","explanation":"if only + had + past participle (strong regret).","explanation_ar":"if only."},{"q":"He didn't read the instructions. (should)  (should have)","options":[],"answer":"He should have read the instructions.","explanation":"should have / shouldn't have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"should have."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Your regrets and wishes.","items":[{"q":"Something you wish you had done last year: ___","options":[],"answer":"I wish I had joined the swimming team last year.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses wish / if only + past perfect for regrets about the past; contrast with wish + past simple for the present; should have / shouldn't have + past participle for criticism and regret correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something you wish you hadn't said: ___","options":[],"answer":"I wish I hadn't said that my cousin's drawing was ugly.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses wish / if only + past perfect for regrets about the past; contrast with wish + past simple for the present; should have / shouldn't have + past participle for criticism and regret correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something you wish about your life now: ___","options":[],"answer":"I wish I had more free time.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses wish / if only + past perfect for regrets about the past; contrast with wish + past simple for the present; should have / shouldn't have + past participle for criticism and regret correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something someone should have done differently: ___","options":[],"answer":"My brother should have checked the tires before the trip.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses wish / if only + past perfect for regrets about the past; contrast with wish + past simple for the present; should have / shouldn't have + past participle for criticism and regret correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"An \"If only…!\" sentence: ___","options":[],"answer":"If only I had saved my game before the power cut!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses wish / if only + past perfect for regrets about the past; contrast with wish + past simple for the present; should have / shouldn't have + past participle for criticism and regret correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Advice from the future.","items":[{"q":"Imagine you are 30. Write 2 regrets about your teenage years with wish.","options":[],"answer":"I wish I had read more books. I wish I hadn't spent so much time on video games.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses wish / if only + past perfect for regrets about the past; contrast with wish + past simple for the present; should have / shouldn't have + past participle for criticism and regret correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences of advice about the past with should have.","options":[],"answer":"I should have learned to cook. I should have spent more time with my grandparents.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses wish / if only + past perfect for regrets about the past; contrast with wish + past simple for the present; should have / shouldn't have + past participle for criticism and regret correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one regret with \"If only\" and one present wish.","options":[],"answer":"If only I had practiced the piano! I wish I could play it now.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses wish / if only + past perfect for regrets about the past; contrast with wish + past simple for the present; should have / shouldn't have + past participle for criticism and regret correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Snakes & Ladders","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Roll and move. If you land on a cue square, make a sentence with the cue and wish / if only + past perfect for regrets about the past; contrast with wish + past simple for the present; should have / shouldn't have + past participle for criticism and regret.","Correct at the bottom of a ladder: climb. Incorrect at the head of a snake: slide down.","Teammates are the judges and must explain any correction.","First player to reach square 30 wins."],"data":[{"cue":"I / study harder / pass the test"},{"cue":"she / not miss the bus / arrive on time"},{"cue":"we / leave earlier / catch the flight"},{"cue":"he / listen to the coach / win the race"},{"cue":"I wish / I / bring an umbrella"},{"cue":"If only / we / not eat so much"},{"cue":"they / check the weather / not get lost"},{"cue":"you / tell me / I / help you"},{"cue":"I should / save my work"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I wish I ___ my phone at home. I needed it all day.","options":["didn't leave","hadn't left","wouldn't leave","haven't left"],"answer":"hadn't left","explanation":"wish + had + past participle for past regrets.","explanation_ar":"wish للندم على الماضي."},{"q":"If only my team ___ the final!","options":["has won","had won","would win","won"],"answer":"had won","explanation":"if only + had + past participle (strong regret).","explanation_ar":"if only."},{"q":"I wish I ___ how to swim. (I can't swim now.)","options":["know","would knew","knew","had known yesterday"],"answer":"knew","explanation":"wish + past simple for a present wish.","explanation_ar":"أمنية الحاضر."},{"q":"","options":["You should had asked for help.","You should have asked for help.","You should asked for help.","You should have ask for help."],"answer":"You should have asked for help.","explanation":"should have / shouldn't have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"should have."},{"q":"","options":["My sister wishes she had chosen biology.","My sister wishes she has chosen biology.","My sister wishes she chose biology last year.","My sister wishes she would have chosen biology."],"answer":"My sister wishes she had chosen biology.","explanation":"wish + had + past participle for past regrets.","explanation_ar":"wish للندم على الماضي."},{"q":"The milk smelled bad. We ___ it.","options":["shouldn't drank","didn't should drink","shouldn't have drunk","shouldn't drink"],"answer":"shouldn't have drunk","explanation":"should have / shouldn't have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"should have."},{"q":"\"I wish I had gone to the museum trip.\" Did the speaker go?","options":["He is going now.","He will go tomorrow.","Yes.","No."],"answer":"No.","explanation":"Past regret or present wish?","explanation_ar":"الماضي أم الحاضر؟"},{"q":"","options":["If only I haven't forgotten Grandma's birthday!","If only I didn't forget Grandma's birthday last week!","If only I wouldn't forget Grandma's birthday yesterday!","If only I hadn't forgotten Grandma's birthday!"],"answer":"If only I hadn't forgotten Grandma's birthday!","explanation":"if only + had + past participle (strong regret).","explanation_ar":"if only."},{"q":"He drove too fast and got a ticket. He ___ more carefully.","options":["should have driven","should have drove","should drive","should drove"],"answer":"should have driven","explanation":"should have / shouldn't have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"should have."},{"q":"Which sentence is a present wish?","options":["I wish I were taller.","I wish I had grown taller as a child.","I should have worn a hat.","I wish I hadn't cut my hair."],"answer":"I wish I were taller.","explanation":"wish + past simple for a present wish.","explanation_ar":"أمنية الحاضر."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"Adam standing in the rain without an umbrella, a thought bubble showing his umbrella at home (\"I wish I had brought it!\"); next to him, Noura looking at a broken vase with \"If only I hadn't run inside!\". Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Adam standing in the rain without an umbrella, a thought bubble showing his umbrella at home (\"I wish I had brought it!\"); next to him, Noura looking at a broken vase with \"If only I hadn't run inside!\""},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of wish / if only + past perfect for regrets about the past; contrast with wish + past simple for the present; should have / shouldn't have + past participle for criticism and regret: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Choices and Consequences”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of wish / if only + past perfect for regrets about the past"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows option (one of the things you can choose); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing option: one of the things you can choose"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows risk (the chance that something bad will happen); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing risk: the chance that something bad will happen"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows priority (the thing that is most important to do first); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing priority: the thing that is most important to do first"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows hesitate (to stop for a moment before you act because you aren't sure); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing hesitate: to stop for a moment before you act because you aren't sure"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Snakes & Ladders”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Snakes & Ladders"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS2-W01","script":"option. option. We have three options for the trip.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS2-W02","script":"risk. risk. Don't take risks when you swim in the sea.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS2-W03","script":"priority. priority. My priority this week is my science project.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS2-W04","script":"hesitate. hesitate. Don't hesitate to ask for help.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I Wish I Had Listened: wish, if only and should have”. Let’s learn wish / if only + past perfect for regrets about the past; contrast with wish + past simple for the present; should have / shouldn't have + past participle for criticism and regret together. Remember these patterns: I wish I had saved my work. If only we hadn't left so late! Do you wish you had chosen a different subject? To talk about regrets about the past, use wish + past perfect: I wish I had listened to my father. (I didn't listen, and now I'm sorry.) If only is stronger and more emotional: If only I hadn't missed the bus! Compare with a present wish: wish + past simple: I wish I had a laptop. (I don't have one now.) Past regret: I wish I had bought that laptop. (I didn't buy it.) Here are some examples. I wish I had brought an umbrella. If only I hadn't eaten that third plate of kabsa! My brother wishes he had studied engineering. Be careful! Some learners say: “I wish I studied harder for yesterday's test.” That’s not right. We say: “I wish I had studied harder for yesterday's test.” Past regret → past perfect. Quick check: \"I wish I had listened to my father.\" Did I listen? … Think! … No. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I wish I had listened to my father.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3","title":"Make a Choice, Face the Consequences: Decision Collocations","objectives":["Students will be able to use decision collocations accurately.","Students will be able to describe people's decision-making with adjectives such as wise, impulsive and reckless.","I can say \"make a decision\", \"take a risk\" and \"face the consequences\".","I can describe someone as wise, impulsive or reckless."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام متلازمات اتخاذ القرار بدقة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من وصف طريقة الناس في اتخاذ القرار بصفات مثل wise وimpulsive وreckless.","أستطيع أن أقول make a decision وtake a risk وface the consequences.","أستطيع أن أصف شخصًا بأنه wise أو impulsive أو reckless."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"peer pressure","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/pɪr ˈprɛʃɚ/","definition":"the influence of friends your age to make you act like them","arabic":"ضغط الأقران","example":"He smoked because of peer pressure, and he regrets it now.","image_id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS3-W01"},{"word":"impulsive","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌɪmˈpʌlsɪv/","definition":"doing things suddenly without thinking first","arabic":"متهوّر / اندفاعي","example":"Impulsive shoppers often buy things they don't need.","image_id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS3-W02"},{"word":"outcome","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈaʊtˌkʌm/","definition":"the final result of an action or event","arabic":"النتيجة النهائية","example":"Nobody could predict the outcome of the match.","image_id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS3-W03"},{"word":"consider","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kənˈsɪdɚ/","definition":"to think carefully about something before deciding","arabic":"يفكّر في / يدرس","example":"Consider all your options before you choose.","image_id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS3-W04"},{"word":"wise","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/waɪz/","definition":"showing good judgment and experience","arabic":"حكيم","example":"My grandfather always gives wise advice.","image_id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS3-W05"},{"word":"reckless","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈrɛkləs/","definition":"not caring about danger or about the results of your actions","arabic":"طائش / غير مبالٍ","example":"Reckless driving causes many accidents.","image_id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-W06","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS3-W06"}],"explanation":{"text":"Decisions have their own collocations. We make a decision, a choice or a plan. We take a risk or a chance. We face or accept the consequences. We weigh the pros and cons and consider the options. We change our mind or have second thoughts.\nMore useful phrases: set priorities, learn a lesson, come to / reach a decision, a tough / difficult / wise choice, a last-minute decision, under pressure, give in to peer pressure, think it over.\nAdjectives for decision-makers: wise (good judgment), responsible (thinks about others and results), impulsive (acts suddenly without thinking), reckless (ignores danger), hesitant (can't decide). Notice: risk (n) → risky (adj); decide (v) → decision (n) → decisive (adj).\nCollocations/phrases: make a decision • make a choice • make up your mind • come to a decision | take a risk • take a chance • face the consequences • accept responsibility | weigh the pros and cons • consider the options • set priorities • think it over | change your mind • have second thoughts • give in to peer pressure • learn a lesson","examples":["It took me a week to make a decision about my summer course.","Don't take risks with your health.","If you cheat, you'll have to face the consequences.","Let's weigh the pros and cons before we buy it.","Adam changed his mind at the last minute.","I'm having second thoughts about the camping trip.","A wise person listens before speaking.","Reckless drivers put everyone in danger."],"common_errors":["✗ I did a decision. → ✓ I made a decision. (make a decision.)","✗ She made a risk. → ✓ She took a risk. (take a risk.)","✗ You must face with the consequences. → ✓ You must face the consequences. (face + noun (no with).)","✗ He changed his opinion and his mind. (meaning: decided differently) → ✓ He changed his mind. (Fixed phrase: change your mind.)"],"arabic":"متلازمات القرار: make a decision (يتخذ قرارًا) وtake a risk (يخاطر) وface the consequences (يواجه العواقب) وweigh the pros and cons (يوازن بين الإيجابيات والسلبيات).\nchange your mind (يغيّر رأيه) وhave second thoughts (يعيد التفكير ويتردد) وset priorities (يحدد أولوياته).\nصفات: wise (حكيم) وimpulsive (اندفاعي) وreckless (طائش) وresponsible (مسؤول).\nنقول make a decision وليس do a decision، وtake a risk وليس make a risk."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Make a Choice, Face the Consequences: Decision Collocations”. Let’s learn collocations and phrases for decisions (make a decision/choice, take a risk, face the consequences, weigh the pros and cons, change your mind, have second thoughts, set priorities); adjectives for decision-makers (wise, impulsive, reckless, responsible) together.","on_screen":"GV-L07-U4-LS3 | Make a Choice, Face the Consequences: Decision Collocations","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. peer pressure: the influence of friends your age to make you act like them. impulsive: doing things suddenly without thinking first. outcome: the final result of an action or event.","on_screen":"peer pressure | impulsive | outcome","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Decisions have their own collocations. We make a decision, a choice or a plan. We take a risk or a chance. We face or accept the consequences. We weigh the pros and cons and consider the options. We change our mind or have second thoughts. More useful phrases: set priorities, learn a lesson, come to / reach a decision, a tough / difficult / wise choice, a last-minute decision, under pressure, give in to peer pressure, think it over.","on_screen":"collocations and phrases for decisions (make a decision/choice, take a risk, face the consequences, weigh the pros and cons, change your mind, have second thoughts, set priorities); adjectives for decision-makers (wise, impulsive, reckless, responsible)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. It took me a week to make a decision about my summer course. Don't take risks with your health. If you cheat, you'll have to face the consequences.","on_screen":"It took me a week to make a decision about my summer course. / Don't take risks with your health. / If you cheat, you'll have to face the consequences.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I did a decision.” That’s not right. We say: “I made a decision.” make a decision.","on_screen":"✗ I did a decision.   ✓ I made a decision.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Do we \"make\" or \"take\" a risk? … Think! … *take* a risk. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"make a decision\", \"take a risk\" and \"face the consequences\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"make a decision\", \"take a risk\" and \"face the consequences\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: collocations and phrases for decisions (make a decision/choice, take a risk, face the consequences, weigh the pros and cons, change your mind, have second thoughts, set priorities); adjectives for decision-makers (wise, impulsive, reckless, responsible).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","متلازمات القرار: make a decision (يتخذ قرارًا) وtake a risk (يخاطر) وface the consequences (يواجه العواقب) وweigh the pros and cons (يوازن بين الإيجابيات والسلبيات).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I did a decision. — الصحيح: I made a decision.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول make a decision وtake a risk وface the consequences."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"You need to ___ a decision before Friday.","options":["get","take on","make","do"],"answer":"make","explanation":"Use the right decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."},{"q":"If you break the rules, you'll have to ___ the consequences.","options":["see","face","look","meet"],"answer":"face","explanation":"Use the right decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."},{"q":"Before you choose, ___ the pros and cons.","options":["balance on","count","measure up","weigh"],"answer":"weigh","explanation":"Use the right decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."},{"q":"Skydiving is exciting, but you ___ a big risk.","options":["make","do","give","take"],"answer":"take","explanation":"Use the right decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."},{"q":"Rakan bought a new phone without thinking for even a second. He's very ___.","options":["patient","impulsive","responsible","wise"],"answer":"impulsive","explanation":"Adjective for a decision-maker.","explanation_ar":"صفة متخذ القرار."},{"q":"Friends sometimes push you to do things you don't want to do. This is ___.","options":["peer pressure","priority","option","outcome"],"answer":"peer pressure","explanation":"Choose the word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the verb to its partner.","items":[{"q":"change","options":["a lesson from a mistake","your priorities for the week","second thoughts about the trip","all the options carefully","your mind at the last minute","to a final decision"],"answer":"your mind at the last minute","explanation":"change → your mind at the last minute. Use the right decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."},{"q":"have","options":["a lesson from a mistake","your priorities for the week","second thoughts about the trip","all the options carefully","your mind at the last minute","to a final decision"],"answer":"second thoughts about the trip","explanation":"have → second thoughts about the trip. Use the right decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."},{"q":"consider","options":["a lesson from a mistake","your priorities for the week","second thoughts about the trip","all the options carefully","your mind at the last minute","to a final decision"],"answer":"all the options carefully","explanation":"consider → all the options carefully. Use the right decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."},{"q":"set","options":["a lesson from a mistake","your priorities for the week","second thoughts about the trip","all the options carefully","your mind at the last minute","to a final decision"],"answer":"your priorities for the week","explanation":"set → your priorities for the week. Use the right decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."},{"q":"learn","options":["a lesson from a mistake","your priorities for the week","second thoughts about the trip","all the options carefully","your mind at the last minute","to a final decision"],"answer":"a lesson from a mistake","explanation":"learn → a lesson from a mistake. Use the right decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."},{"q":"come","options":["a lesson from a mistake","your priorities for the week","second thoughts about the trip","all the options carefully","your mind at the last minute","to a final decision"],"answer":"to a final decision","explanation":"come → to a final decision. Use the right decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Talk about decisions.","items":[{"q":"A big decision you made this year: ___","options":[],"answer":"I made a decision to change my elective to computer science.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses collocations and phrases for decisions (make a decision/choice, take a risk, face the consequences, weigh the pros and cons, change your mind, have second thoughts, set priorities); adjectives for decision-makers (wise, impulsive, reckless, responsible) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A risk you would never take: ___","options":[],"answer":"I would never take a risk with fire.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses collocations and phrases for decisions (make a decision/choice, take a risk, face the consequences, weigh the pros and cons, change your mind, have second thoughts, set priorities); adjectives for decision-makers (wise, impulsive, reckless, responsible) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A time you changed your mind: ___","options":[],"answer":"I changed my mind about the trip because my grandmother was sick.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses collocations and phrases for decisions (make a decision/choice, take a risk, face the consequences, weigh the pros and cons, change your mind, have second thoughts, set priorities); adjectives for decision-makers (wise, impulsive, reckless, responsible) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Your top priority this month: ___","options":[],"answer":"My top priority this month is preparing for the math olympiad.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses collocations and phrases for decisions (make a decision/choice, take a risk, face the consequences, weigh the pros and cons, change your mind, have second thoughts, set priorities); adjectives for decision-makers (wise, impulsive, reckless, responsible) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Describe a wise person you know.","options":[],"answer":"My grandfather is wise because he always thinks before he speaks.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses collocations and phrases for decisions (make a decision/choice, take a risk, face the consequences, weigh the pros and cons, change your mind, have second thoughts, set priorities); adjectives for decision-makers (wise, impulsive, reckless, responsible) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Decision guide.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 steps for making a good decision, using 3 collocations.","options":[],"answer":"First, consider all the options. Then weigh the pros and cons. Finally, think it over before you make a decision.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses collocations and phrases for decisions (make a decision/choice, take a risk, face the consequences, weigh the pros and cons, change your mind, have second thoughts, set priorities); adjectives for decision-makers (wise, impulsive, reckless, responsible) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences comparing an impulsive person and a wise person.","options":[],"answer":"An impulsive person buys things immediately. A wise person waits and compares prices.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses collocations and phrases for decisions (make a decision/choice, take a risk, face the consequences, weigh the pros and cons, change your mind, have second thoughts, set priorities); adjectives for decision-makers (wise, impulsive, reckless, responsible) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence about peer pressure.","options":[],"answer":"Don't give in to peer pressure; make your own choices.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses collocations and phrases for decisions (make a decision/choice, take a risk, face the consequences, weigh the pros and cons, change your mind, have second thoughts, set priorities); adjectives for decision-makers (wise, impulsive, reckless, responsible) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Dominoes","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Deal the dominoes equally in teams of four.","Player 1 places a domino; the next player adds a domino whose word matches the open definition.","If you cannot play, pass.","The first player with no dominoes left wins."],"data":[{"word":"consequence","match":"a result of an action, often a bad one","arabic":"عاقبة / نتيجة"},{"word":"regret","match":"to feel sorry about something you did or didn't do","arabic":"يندم على"},{"word":"decision","match":"a choice you make after thinking","arabic":"قرار"},{"word":"choice","match":"the act of choosing, or something you choose","arabic":"اختيار"},{"word":"option","match":"one of the things you can choose","arabic":"خيار / بديل"},{"word":"risk","match":"the chance that something bad will happen","arabic":"مخاطرة"},{"word":"priority","match":"the thing that is most important to do first","arabic":"أولوية"},{"word":"hesitate","match":"to stop for a moment before you act because you aren't sure","arabic":"يتردّد"},{"word":"peer pressure","match":"the influence of friends your age to make you act like them","arabic":"ضغط الأقران"},{"word":"impulsive","match":"doing things suddenly without thinking first","arabic":"متهوّر / اندفاعي"},{"word":"outcome","match":"the final result of an action or event","arabic":"النتيجة النهائية"},{"word":"consider","match":"to think carefully about something before deciding","arabic":"يفكّر في / يدرس"},{"word":"wise","match":"showing good judgment and experience","arabic":"حكيم"},{"word":"reckless","match":"not caring about danger or about the results of your actions","arabic":"طائش / غير مبالٍ"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"After a long discussion, the family finally came ___ a decision.","options":["on","in","to","at"],"answer":"to","explanation":"Use the right decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."},{"q":"I was going to join the trip, but now I'm having second ___.","options":["choices","ideas","thoughts","minds"],"answer":"thoughts","explanation":"Fixed phrase (change your mind, second thoughts).","explanation_ar":"العبارة الثابتة."},{"q":"He drives at 200 km/h on the highway. He's ___.","options":["wise","reckless","hesitant","responsible"],"answer":"reckless","explanation":"Adjective for a decision-maker.","explanation_ar":"صفة متخذ القرار."},{"q":"When you are a captain, you have to accept ___ for the team.","options":["responsibly","responsible","respond","responsibility"],"answer":"responsibility","explanation":"Use the right decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."},{"q":"Investing all your money in one company is very ___.","options":["risked","risk","riskily","risky"],"answer":"risky","explanation":"Adjective for a decision-maker.","explanation_ar":"صفة متخذ القرار."},{"q":"The ___ of the vote surprised everyone.","options":["outcome","pressure","option","priority"],"answer":"outcome","explanation":"Choose the word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Don't ___ to ask questions if you don't understand.","options":["consider","hesitate","regret","weigh"],"answer":"hesitate","explanation":"Choose the word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"I wanted pizza, but then I ___ my mind and ordered salad.","options":["changed","took","turned","made"],"answer":"changed","explanation":"Fixed phrase (change your mind, second thoughts).","explanation_ar":"العبارة الثابتة."},{"q":"","options":["Let's think it over before we decide.","Let's think it about before we decide.","Let's think over it before we decide.","Let's think it on before we decide."],"answer":"Let's think it over before we decide.","explanation":"Fixed phrase (change your mind, second thoughts).","explanation_ar":"العبارة الثابتة."},{"q":"He didn't plan; he made a ___ decision.","options":["late-minutely","last-minute","lastly-minute","last minute's"],"answer":"last-minute","explanation":"Use the right decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A teenager standing at a crossroads sign with arrows labelled \"Option A\", \"Option B\" and \"Option C\"; a balance scale with \"pros\" and \"cons\"; friends behind him whispering (peer pressure) and a wise grandfather on a bench. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A teenager standing at a crossroads sign with arrows labelled \"Option A\", \"Option B\" and \"Option C\"; a balance scale with \"pros\" and \"cons\"; friends behind him whispering (peer pressure) and a wise grandfather on a bench"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows peer pressure (the influence of friends your age to make you act like them); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing peer pressure: the influence of friends your age to make you act like them"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows impulsive (doing things suddenly without thinking first); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing impulsive: doing things suddenly without thinking first"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows outcome (the final result of an action or event); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing outcome: the final result of an action or event"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows consider (to think carefully about something before deciding); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing consider: to think carefully about something before deciding"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows wise (showing good judgment and experience); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing wise: showing good judgment and experience"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-W06","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows reckless (not caring about danger or about the results of your actions); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing reckless: not caring about danger or about the results of your actions"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Dominoes”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Dominoes"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS3-W01","script":"peer pressure. peer pressure. He smoked because of peer pressure, and he regrets it now.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS3-W02","script":"impulsive. impulsive. Impulsive shoppers often buy things they don't need.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS3-W03","script":"outcome. outcome. Nobody could predict the outcome of the match.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS3-W04","script":"consider. consider. Consider all your options before you choose.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS3-W05","script":"wise. wise. My grandfather always gives wise advice.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS3-W06","script":"reckless. reckless. Reckless driving causes many accidents.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Make a Choice, Face the Consequences: Decision Collocations”. Let’s learn collocations and phrases for decisions (make a decision/choice, take a risk, face the consequences, weigh the pros and cons, change your mind, have second thoughts, set priorities); adjectives for decision-makers (wise, impulsive, reckless, responsible) together. Meet some new words. peer pressure: the influence of friends your age to make you act like them. impulsive: doing things suddenly without thinking first. outcome: the final result of an action or event. Decisions have their own collocations. We make a decision, a choice or a plan. We take a risk or a chance. We face or accept the consequences. We weigh the pros and cons and consider the options. We change our mind or have second thoughts. More useful phrases: set priorities, learn a lesson, come to / reach a decision, a tough / difficult / wise choice, a last-minute decision, under pressure, give in to peer pressure, think it over. Here are some examples. It took me a week to make a decision about my summer course. Don't take risks with your health. If you cheat, you'll have to face the consequences. Be careful! Some learners say: “I did a decision.” That’s not right. We say: “I made a decision.” make a decision. Quick check: Do we \"make\" or \"take\" a risk? … Think! … *take* a risk. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"make a decision\", \"take a risk\" and \"face the consequences\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS4","title":"Walking to School, the Rain Started? Misplaced and Dangling Modifiers","objectives":["Students will be able to find misplaced and dangling modifiers.","Students will be able to fix them by moving the modifier or adding the correct subject.","I can explain why \"Walking to school, the rain started\" is wrong.","I can put \"only\" and \"almost\" in the right place."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من اكتشاف المُعدِّلات في غير موضعها والمُعدِّلات المعلّقة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من تصحيحها بنقل المُعدِّل أو إضافة الفاعل الصحيح.","أستطيع أن أشرح لماذا Walking to school, the rain started خطأ.","أستطيع أن أضع only وalmost في المكان الصحيح."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"consequence","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɑnsəkwəns/","definition":"a result of an action, often a bad one","arabic":"عاقبة / نتيجة","example":"Every choice has consequences.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"regret","pos":"verb","ipa":"/rəˈɡrɛt/","definition":"to feel sorry about something you did or didn't do","arabic":"يندم على","example":"I regret not saying goodbye to my teacher.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"decision","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dɪˈsɪʒən/","definition":"a choice you make after thinking","arabic":"قرار","example":"Choosing a university is a big decision.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"choice","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tʃɔɪs/","definition":"the act of choosing, or something you choose","arabic":"اختيار","example":"You made a wise choice.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"option","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɑpʃən/","definition":"one of the things you can choose","arabic":"خيار / بديل","example":"We have three options for the trip.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"risk","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rɪsk/","definition":"the chance that something bad will happen","arabic":"مخاطرة","example":"Don't take risks when you swim in the sea.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"A modifier is a word or phrase that describes something. Put it next to the word it describes. A misplaced modifier is in the wrong place, so the meaning becomes strange: (not: We saw a camel driving to Al-Ula.) (The camel was driving?) → Driving to Al-Ula, we saw a camel.\nA dangling modifier is an opening phrase (often with -ing, -ed or after/while + -ing) that has no logical subject in the main clause: (not: Walking to school, the rain started.) (The rain was walking?) Fix it by making the subject the person who does the action: Walking to school, I got caught in the rain. Or change the phrase into a clause: While I was walking to school, the rain started.\nSmall words like only, almost, just, nearly change meaning by position: I almost failed every test. (I passed them all, just barely.) ↔ I failed almost every test. (I failed most of them.)\nPut the modifier next to the word it describes.\nOpening -ing / -ed phrase → the next word must be the doer.\nFix: move the modifier • add the right subject • turn the phrase into a clause\nonly / almost / just / nearly → right before the word they limit","examples":["Walking to school, I got caught in the rain.","While I was walking to school, the rain started.","After I finished the exam, the bell rang.","She bought a phone with a cracked screen from a website.","Tired after the match, the players sat down.","I failed almost every test last term.","Only Faisal knew the answer. (nobody else)","The mailman ran from our dog, which was barking loudly."],"common_errors":["✗ Walking to school, the rain started. → ✓ Walking to school, I got caught in the rain. (The rain wasn't walking → add the doer.)","✗ After finishing the exam, the bell rang. → ✓ After I finished the exam, the bell rang. (The bell didn't finish the exam.)","✗ She bought a phone from a website with a cracked screen. → ✓ She bought a phone with a cracked screen from a website. (The phone had the cracked screen.)","✗ I almost ate the whole pizza. (I ate 90% of it) → ✓ I ate almost the whole pizza. (almost goes before the whole pizza.)"],"arabic":"المُعدِّل كلمة أو عبارة تصف شيئًا، ويجب أن يأتي بجوار ما يصفه.\nالمُعدِّل في غير موضعه (misplaced) يغيّر المعنى: We saw a camel driving to Al-Ula (كأن الجمل يقود!).\nالمُعدِّل المعلّق (dangling) عبارة في أول الجملة بلا فاعل منطقي: Walking to school, the rain started (كأن المطر يمشي!). الصواب: Walking to school, I got caught in the rain.\nمكان only وalmost وjust يغيّر المعنى، فنضعها قبل الكلمة التي تحددها مباشرة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Walking to School, the Rain Started? Misplaced and Dangling Modifiers”. Let’s learn misplaced modifiers (words and phrases in the wrong place, including only, almost, just, nearly) and dangling modifiers (opening phrases with no logical subject); how to fix them together.","on_screen":"GV-L07-U4-LS4 | Walking to School, the Rain Started? Misplaced and Dangling Modifiers","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"A modifier is a word or phrase that describes something. Put it next to the word it describes. A misplaced modifier is in the wrong place, so the meaning becomes strange: (not: We saw a camel driving to Al-Ula.) (The camel was driving?) → Driving to Al-Ula, we saw a camel.","on_screen":"misplaced modifiers (words and phrases in the wrong place, including only, almost, just, nearly) and dangling modifiers (opening phrases with no logical subject); how to fix them","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"A modifier is a word or phrase that describes something. Put it next to the word it describes. A misplaced modifier is in the wrong place, so the meaning becomes strange: (not: We saw a camel driving to Al-Ula.) (The camel was driving?) → Driving to Al-Ula, we saw a camel. A dangling modifier is an opening phrase (often with -ing, -ed or after/while + -ing) that has no logical subject in the main clause: (not: Walking to school, the rain started.) (The rain was walking?) Fix it by making the subject the person who does the action: Walking to school, I got caught in the rain. Or change the phrase into a clause: While I was walking to school, the rain started.","on_screen":"Put the modifier next to the word it describes. • Opening -ing / -ed phrase → the next word must be the doer. • Fix: move the modifier • add the right subject • turn the phrase into a clause","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Walking to school, I got caught in the rain. While I was walking to school, the rain started. After I finished the exam, the bell rang.","on_screen":"Walking to school, I got caught in the rain. / While I was walking to school, the rain started. / After I finished the exam, the bell rang.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Walking to school, the rain started.” That’s not right. We say: “Walking to school, I got caught in the rain.” The rain wasn't walking → add the doer.","on_screen":"✗ Walking to school, the rain started.   ✓ Walking to school, I got caught in the rain.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"Walking to school, the rain started.\" Who was walking? … Think! … The sentence says the rain – that's the problem! Great job! Now you can say: I can explain why \"Walking to school, the rain started\" is wrong.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can explain why \"Walking to school, the rain started\" is wrong.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: misplaced modifiers (words and phrases in the wrong place, including only, almost, just, nearly) and dangling modifiers (opening phrases with no logical subject); how to fix them.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","المُعدِّل كلمة أو عبارة تصف شيئًا، ويجب أن يأتي بجوار ما يصفه.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Walking to school, the rain started. — الصحيح: Walking to school, I got caught in the rain.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أشرح لماذا Walking to school, the rain started خطأ."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"A Bad Morning (editing passage)","body":"Having stayed up all night, my eyes would not stay open. Looking at the clock, it was already 7:30. I almost ate nothing for breakfast. Running to the bus stop, my shoe came off. Arriving at school, my homework was missing. I had left it on the kitchen table!","word_count":49,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["Walking to school, the rain caught me.","Walking to school, rain was falling on me.","Walking to school, I got caught in the rain.","Walking to school, the rain started."],"answer":"Walking to school, I got caught in the rain.","explanation":"Opening phrase needs the right subject.","explanation_ar":"العبارة الافتتاحية تحتاج الفاعل الصحيح."},{"q":"Saad failed nine out of ten tests. Which sentence says this correctly?","options":["Almost Saad failed every test.","Saad failed almost every test.","Saad almost failed every test.","Saad failed every almost test."],"answer":"Saad failed almost every test.","explanation":"Put only / almost / just / nearly before the word they limit.","explanation_ar":"مكان only وalmost."},{"q":"","options":["After finishing, the exam the bell rang.","After finishing the exam, the bell rang.","Having finished the exam, the bell rang.","After I finished the exam, the bell rang."],"answer":"After I finished the exam, the bell rang.","explanation":"Opening phrase needs the right subject.","explanation_ar":"العبارة الافتتاحية تحتاج الفاعل الصحيح."},{"q":"","options":["She with a cracked screen bought a phone from a website.","With a cracked screen, she bought a phone from a website.","She bought a phone with a cracked screen from a website.","She bought a phone from a website with a cracked screen."],"answer":"She bought a phone with a cracked screen from a website.","explanation":"Move the modifier next to the word it describes.","explanation_ar":"انقل المُعدِّل بجوار ما يصفه."},{"q":"What does \"Only I have ten riyals\" mean?","options":["I have ten riyals only today.","I have ten riyals and some coins.","I have no more than ten riyals.","Nobody else has ten riyals."],"answer":"Nobody else has ten riyals.","explanation":"Put only / almost / just / nearly before the word they limit.","explanation_ar":"مكان only وalmost."},{"q":"What is wrong with \"Covered in chocolate, my mother gave me the cake\"?","options":["It sounds like my mother was covered in chocolate.","Nothing is wrong.","The verb is in the wrong tense.","It needs a question mark."],"answer":"It sounds like my mother was covered in chocolate.","explanation":"Move the modifier next to the word it describes.","explanation_ar":"انقل المُعدِّل بجوار ما يصفه."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite the sentences to fix the modifiers.","items":[{"q":"Running for the bus, my bag fell open.  (fix)","options":[],"answer":"While I was running for the bus, my bag fell open.","explanation":"Opening phrase needs the right subject.","explanation_ar":"العبارة الافتتاحية تحتاج الفاعل الصحيح."},{"q":"We saw a camel driving to Al-Ula.  (fix)","options":[],"answer":"Driving to Al-Ula, we saw a camel.","explanation":"Move the modifier next to the word it describes.","explanation_ar":"انقل المُعدِّل بجوار ما يصفه."},{"q":"Having eaten lunch, the movie began.  (fix)","options":[],"answer":"After we had eaten lunch, the movie began.","explanation":"Opening phrase needs the right subject.","explanation_ar":"العبارة الافتتاحية تحتاج الفاعل الصحيح."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS4-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the sentences.","items":[{"q":"Barking loudly, the mailman ran from our dog.","options":[],"answer":"The mailman ran from our dog, which was barking loudly.","explanation":"Barking loudly, the mailman ran from our dog. → The mailman ran from our dog, which was barking loudly.. Move the modifier next to the word it describes.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Barking loudly, the mailman ran from our dog. → The mailman ran from our dog, which was barking loudly.. انقل المُعدِّل بجوار ما يصفه."},{"q":"Tired after the match, the bed looked wonderful.","options":[],"answer":"Tired after the match, I thought the bed looked wonderful.","explanation":"Tired after the match, the bed looked wonderful. → Tired after the match, I thought the bed looked wonderful.. Opening phrase needs the right subject.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Tired after the match, the bed looked wonderful. → Tired after the match, I thought the bed looked wonderful.. العبارة الافتتاحية تحتاج الفاعل الصحيح."},{"q":"My grandmother served kabsa to the guests on large plates.","options":[],"answer":"My grandmother served kabsa on large plates to the guests.","explanation":"My grandmother served kabsa to the guests on large plates. → My grandmother served kabsa on large plates to the guests.. Move the modifier next to the word it describes.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: My grandmother served kabsa to the guests on large plates. → My grandmother served kabsa on large plates to the guests.. انقل المُعدِّل بجوار ما يصفه."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the story.","items":[{"q":"Having stayed up all night, my eyes would not stay open. Looking at the clock, I saw that it was already 7:30. I ate almost nothing for breakfast. While I was running to the bus stop, my shoe came off. Arriving at school, I realized that my homework was missing. I had left it on the kitchen table!","options":[],"answer":"Having stayed up all night, I couldn't keep my eyes open. Looking at the clock, I saw that it was already 7:30. I ate almost nothing for breakfast. While I was running to the bus stop, my shoe came off. Arriving at school, I realized that my homework was missing. I had left it on the kitchen table!","explanation":"Having stayed up all night, my eyes would not stay open. → Having stayed up all night, I couldn't keep my eyes open.. Move the modifier next to the word it describes.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Having stayed up all night, my eyes would not stay open. → Having stayed up all night, I couldn't keep my eyes open.. انقل المُعدِّل بجوار ما يصفه."},{"q":"Having stayed up all night, I couldn't keep my eyes open. Looking at the clock, it was already 7:30. I ate almost nothing for breakfast. While I was running to the bus stop, my shoe came off. Arriving at school, I realized that my homework was missing. I had left it on the kitchen table!","options":[],"answer":"Having stayed up all night, I couldn't keep my eyes open. Looking at the clock, I saw that it was already 7:30. I ate almost nothing for breakfast. While I was running to the bus stop, my shoe came off. Arriving at school, I realized that my homework was missing. I had left it on the kitchen table!","explanation":"Looking at the clock, it was already 7:30. → Looking at the clock, I saw that it was already 7:30.. Move the modifier next to the word it describes.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Looking at the clock, it was already 7:30. → Looking at the clock, I saw that it was already 7:30.. انقل المُعدِّل بجوار ما يصفه."},{"q":"Having stayed up all night, I couldn't keep my eyes open. Looking at the clock, I saw that it was already 7:30. I almost ate nothing for breakfast. While I was running to the bus stop, my shoe came off. Arriving at school, I realized that my homework was missing. I had left it on the kitchen table!","options":[],"answer":"Having stayed up all night, I couldn't keep my eyes open. Looking at the clock, I saw that it was already 7:30. I ate almost nothing for breakfast. While I was running to the bus stop, my shoe came off. Arriving at school, I realized that my homework was missing. I had left it on the kitchen table!","explanation":"almost ate nothing → ate almost nothing. Move the modifier next to the word it describes.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: almost ate nothing → ate almost nothing. انقل المُعدِّل بجوار ما يصفه."},{"q":"Having stayed up all night, I couldn't keep my eyes open. Looking at the clock, I saw that it was already 7:30. I ate almost nothing for breakfast. Running to the bus stop, my shoe came off. Arriving at school, I realized that my homework was missing. I had left it on the kitchen table!","options":[],"answer":"Having stayed up all night, I couldn't keep my eyes open. Looking at the clock, I saw that it was already 7:30. I ate almost nothing for breakfast. While I was running to the bus stop, my shoe came off. Arriving at school, I realized that my homework was missing. I had left it on the kitchen table!","explanation":"Running to the bus stop, my shoe came off. → While I was running to the bus stop, my shoe came off.. Move the modifier next to the word it describes.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Running to the bus stop, my shoe came off. → While I was running to the bus stop, my shoe came off.. انقل المُعدِّل بجوار ما يصفه."},{"q":"Having stayed up all night, I couldn't keep my eyes open. Looking at the clock, I saw that it was already 7:30. I ate almost nothing for breakfast. While I was running to the bus stop, my shoe came off. Arriving at school, my homework was missing. I had left it on the kitchen table!","options":[],"answer":"Having stayed up all night, I couldn't keep my eyes open. Looking at the clock, I saw that it was already 7:30. I ate almost nothing for breakfast. While I was running to the bus stop, my shoe came off. Arriving at school, I realized that my homework was missing. I had left it on the kitchen table!","explanation":"Arriving at school, my homework was missing. → Arriving at school, I realized that my homework was missing.. Move the modifier next to the word it describes.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Arriving at school, my homework was missing. → Arriving at school, I realized that my homework was missing.. انقل المُعدِّل بجوار ما يصفه."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write clear sentences.","items":[{"q":"Write a correct sentence that starts with an -ing phrase.","options":[],"answer":"Looking out of the window, Lina saw a falcon.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses misplaced modifiers (words and phrases in the wrong place, including only, almost, just, nearly) and dangling modifiers (opening phrases with no logical subject); how to fix them correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write two sentences with \"only\" in different places and explain the difference.","options":[],"answer":"Only Omar ate the dates. (Nobody else ate them.) Omar ate only the dates. (He didn't eat anything else.)","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses misplaced modifiers (words and phrases in the wrong place, including only, almost, just, nearly) and dangling modifiers (opening phrases with no logical subject); how to fix them correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Fix this sentence and explain the problem: \"Opening the door, the cat ran out.\"","options":[],"answer":"Opening the door, I saw the cat run out. The cat didn't open the door.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses misplaced modifiers (words and phrases in the wrong place, including only, almost, just, nearly) and dangling modifiers (opening phrases with no logical subject); how to fix them correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Speed Spell","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a word and a short sentence with it.","Students write the word in 10 seconds.","Show boards on \"Show me!\". Correct = 1 point.","After 10 words, partners check each other's boards and correct any mistakes."],"data":[{"word":"consequence","clue":"a result of an action, often a bad one"},{"word":"decision","clue":"a choice you make after thinking"},{"word":"priority","clue":"the thing that is most important to do first"},{"word":"hesitate","clue":"to stop for a moment before you act because you aren't sure"},{"word":"responsible","clue":""},{"word":"reckless","clue":"not caring about danger or about the results of your actions"},{"word":"regret","clue":"to feel sorry about something you did or didn't do"},{"word":"choice","clue":"the act of choosing, or something you choose"},{"word":"option","clue":"one of the things you can choose"},{"word":"risk","clue":"the chance that something bad will happen"},{"word":"impulsive","clue":"doing things suddenly without thinking first"},{"word":"outcome","clue":"the final result of an action or event"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["Looking through the telescope, we saw Saturn's rings.","Looking through the telescope, the rings of Saturn shone.","Looking through the telescope, Saturn's rings were visible.","Looking through the telescope, Saturn's rings appeared."],"answer":"Looking through the telescope, we saw Saturn's rings.","explanation":"Opening phrase needs the right subject.","explanation_ar":"العبارة الافتتاحية تحتاج الفاعل الصحيح."},{"q":"","options":["While doing my homework, the lights went out.","Having done my homework, the lights went out.","While I was doing my homework, the lights went out.","Doing my homework, the lights went out."],"answer":"While I was doing my homework, the lights went out.","explanation":"Opening phrase needs the right subject.","explanation_ar":"العبارة الافتتاحية تحتاج الفاعل الصحيح."},{"q":"My brother drank 90% of the juice. Which sentence is correct?","options":["My brother drank almost all the juice.","My brother drank all almost the juice.","My brother almost drank all the juice.","Almost my brother drank all the juice."],"answer":"My brother drank almost all the juice.","explanation":"Put only / almost / just / nearly before the word they limit.","explanation_ar":"مكان only وalmost."},{"q":"","options":["The boy lost his wallet with a red hat in the park.","The boy with a red hat lost his wallet in the park.","The boy lost his wallet in the park with a red hat.","With a red hat in the park, the boy lost his wallet."],"answer":"The boy with a red hat lost his wallet in the park.","explanation":"Move the modifier next to the word it describes.","explanation_ar":"انقل المُعدِّل بجوار ما يصفه."},{"q":"Which sentence has a dangling modifier?","options":["After the hike, we drank tea.","Exhausted from the hike, we drank some hot tea.","We were exhausted from the hike.","Exhausted from the hike, the hot tea tasted wonderful."],"answer":"Exhausted from the hike, the hot tea tasted wonderful.","explanation":"Opening phrase needs the right subject.","explanation_ar":"العبارة الافتتاحية تحتاج الفاعل الصحيح."},{"q":"\"Just Adam passed the test.\" What does it mean?","options":["Adam barely passed.","Adam passed a moment ago.","Adam was the only one who passed.","Adam passed fairly."],"answer":"Adam was the only one who passed.","explanation":"Put only / almost / just / nearly before the word they limit.","explanation_ar":"مكان only وalmost."},{"q":"","options":["I read about the new museum printed in the newspaper hall.","In the newspaper, I read about the new museum that was printed.","I read in the new museum about the newspaper.","I read about the new museum in the newspaper."],"answer":"I read about the new museum in the newspaper.","explanation":"Move the modifier next to the word it describes.","explanation_ar":"انقل المُعدِّل بجوار ما يصفه."},{"q":"How can we fix \"Having lost the match, the bus ride home was quiet.\"?","options":["Having lost, the bus ride home was quiet.","The bus ride, having lost the match, was quiet.","Having lost the match, the bus was quiet.","Having lost the match, we were quiet on the bus ride home."],"answer":"Having lost the match, we were quiet on the bus ride home.","explanation":"Choose the best correction.","explanation_ar":"أفضل تصحيح."},{"q":"Which sentence is clear and correct?","options":["Driving through Abha, the green mountains amazed.","Driving through Abha, the green mountains were admired.","Driving through Abha, we admired the green mountains.","Driving through Abha, the mountains looked green to us."],"answer":"Driving through Abha, we admired the green mountains.","explanation":"Choose the best correction.","explanation_ar":"أفضل تصحيح."},{"q":"","options":["Hamad scored nearly three goals. (He hit the post three times.)","Hamad nearly scored three goals. (He scored none – he hit the post three times.)","Hamad scored three nearly goals. (He hit the post three times.)","Nearly Hamad scored three goals. (He hit the post three times.)"],"answer":"Hamad nearly scored three goals. (He scored none – he hit the post three times.)","explanation":"Put only / almost / just / nearly before the word they limit.","explanation_ar":"مكان only وalmost."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Choices and Consequences” that shows misplaced modifiers (words and phrases in the wrong place, including only, almost, just, nearly) and dangling modifiers (opening phrases with no logical subject); how to fix them in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Choices and Consequences” that shows misplaced modifiers (words and phrases in the wrong place, including only, almost, just, nearly) and dangling modifiers (opening phrases with no logical subject); how to fix them in action"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Speed Spell”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Speed Spell"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Walking to School, the Rain Started? Misplaced and Dangling Modifiers”. Let’s learn misplaced modifiers (words and phrases in the wrong place, including only, almost, just, nearly) and dangling modifiers (opening phrases with no logical subject); how to fix them together. A modifier is a word or phrase that describes something. Put it next to the word it describes. A misplaced modifier is in the wrong place, so the meaning becomes strange: (not: We saw a camel driving to Al-Ula.) (The camel was driving?) → Driving to Al-Ula, we saw a camel. A modifier is a word or phrase that describes something. Put it next to the word it describes. A misplaced modifier is in the wrong place, so the meaning becomes strange: (not: We saw a camel driving to Al-Ula.) (The camel was driving?) → Driving to Al-Ula, we saw a camel. A dangling modifier is an opening phrase (often with -ing, -ed or after/while + -ing) that has no logical subject in the main clause: (not: Walking to school, the rain started.) (The rain was walking?) Fix it by making the subject the person who does the action: Walking to school, I got caught in the rain. Or change the phrase into a clause: While I was walking to school, the rain started. Here are some examples. Walking to school, I got caught in the rain. While I was walking to school, the rain started. After I finished the exam, the bell rang. Be careful! Some learners say: “Walking to school, the rain started.” That’s not right. We say: “Walking to school, I got caught in the rain.” The rain wasn't walking → add the doer. Quick check: \"Walking to school, the rain started.\" Who was walking? … Think! … The sentence says the rain – that's the problem! Great job! Now you can say: I can explain why \"Walking to school, the rain started\" is wrong.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS5","title":"The Choice I Wish I Had Made: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to discuss real and imaginary choices and their consequences.","Students will be able to write a reflective paragraph about a decision using the third conditional, regrets and clear modifiers.","I can talk about a choice I regret and what I learned.","I can write a reflection on a decision."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من مناقشة خيارات حقيقية ومتخيَّلة ونتائجها.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة فقرة تأملية عن قرار باستخدام الشرط الثالث والندم والمُعدِّلات الواضحة.","أستطيع أن أتحدث عن اختيار أندم عليه وما تعلّمته منه.","أستطيع أن أكتب تأملًا في قرار اتخذته."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"consequence","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɑnsəkwəns/","definition":"a result of an action, often a bad one","arabic":"عاقبة / نتيجة","example":"Every choice has consequences.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"regret","pos":"verb","ipa":"/rəˈɡrɛt/","definition":"to feel sorry about something you did or didn't do","arabic":"يندم على","example":"I regret not saying goodbye to my teacher.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"decision","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dɪˈsɪʒən/","definition":"a choice you make after thinking","arabic":"قرار","example":"Choosing a university is a big decision.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"choice","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tʃɔɪs/","definition":"the act of choosing, or something you choose","arabic":"اختيار","example":"You made a wise choice.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"option","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɑpʃən/","definition":"one of the things you can choose","arabic":"خيار / بديل","example":"We have three options for the trip.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"risk","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rɪsk/","definition":"the chance that something bad will happen","arabic":"مخاطرة","example":"Don't take risks when you swim in the sea.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"priority","pos":"noun","ipa":"/praɪˈɔrəti/","definition":"the thing that is most important to do first","arabic":"أولوية","example":"My priority this week is my science project.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"hesitate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈhɛzəˌteɪt/","definition":"to stop for a moment before you act because you aren't sure","arabic":"يتردّد","example":"Don't hesitate to ask for help.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"peer pressure","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/pɪr ˈprɛʃɚ/","definition":"the influence of friends your age to make you act like them","arabic":"ضغط الأقران","example":"He smoked because of peer pressure, and he regrets it now.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"impulsive","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌɪmˈpʌlsɪv/","definition":"doing things suddenly without thinking first","arabic":"متهوّر / اندفاعي","example":"Impulsive shoppers often buy things they don't need.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"outcome","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈaʊtˌkʌm/","definition":"the final result of an action or event","arabic":"النتيجة النهائية","example":"Nobody could predict the outcome of the match.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"consider","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kənˈsɪdɚ/","definition":"to think carefully about something before deciding","arabic":"يفكّر في / يدرس","example":"Consider all your options before you choose.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"wise","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/waɪz/","definition":"showing good judgment and experience","arabic":"حكيم","example":"My grandfather always gives wise advice.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"reckless","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈrɛkləs/","definition":"not caring about danger or about the results of your actions","arabic":"طائش / غير مبالٍ","example":"Reckless driving causes many accidents.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 4: the third conditional, wish / if only + past perfect, should have, decision collocations and clear modifiers.\nA reflection tells what happened, how it could have been different (third conditional), how you feel about it (wish / if only), what you should have done and what you learned.\n✔ If + had done, would/could/might have done\n✔ wish / if only + had done • should(n't) have done\n✔ make a decision, consider the options, weigh the pros and cons\n✔ opening -ing phrase + the doer as subject","examples":["If I had asked for help, I wouldn't have wasted so much time.","I wish I had chosen a different topic.","If only we had started earlier!","I should have considered all the options.","Feeling nervous, I forgot my first line.","I took a risk, and it didn't work.","I learned an important lesson from that mistake.","Next time, I'll think it over before I decide."],"common_errors":["✗ If I would have researched more, I would have found a better project. → ✓ If I had researched more, … (No would in the if-clause.)","✗ I wish I listened to Lina last year. → ✓ I wish I had listened to Lina last year. (Past regret → past perfect.)","✗ Rushing through the experiment, the mixture became too thick. → ✓ Rushing through the experiment, I made the mixture too thick. (Dangling modifier → add the doer.)"],"arabic":"نراجع الشرط الثالث وwish وif only وshould have ومتلازمات القرار والمُعدِّلات الواضحة.\nالتأمل يذكر: ماذا حدث، وكيف كان يمكن أن يكون مختلفًا، وبماذا تشعر، وماذا كان يجب أن تفعل، وماذا تعلّمت.\nتذكّر: لا would بعد if، والماضي التام بعد wish للندم، والفاعل الصحيح بعد عبارة ing."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Choice I Wish I Had Made: Language in Use”. Let’s learn third conditional, wish / if only / should have, decision collocations, clear modifiers (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L07-U4-LS5 | The Choice I Wish I Had Made: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Decision story circle: in groups of four, each student tells a short story about a choice (real or imaginary). The group responds with one third conditional sentence, one \"I wish…\" sentence and one \"He should have…\" sentence. Choose the best story to share with the class.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 4: the third conditional, wish / if only + past perfect, should have, decision collocations and clear modifiers. A reflection tells what happened, how it could have been different (third conditional), how you feel about it (wish / if only), what you should have done and what you learned.","on_screen":"✔ If + had done, would/could/might have done • ✔ wish / if only + had done • should(n't) have done • ✔ make a decision, consider the options, weigh the pros and cons","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. If I had asked for help, I wouldn't have wasted so much time. I wish I had chosen a different topic. If only we had started earlier!","on_screen":"If I had asked for help, I wouldn't have wasted so much time. / I wish I had chosen a different topic. / If only we had started earlier!","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “If I would have researched more, I would have found a better project.” That’s not right. We say: “If I had researched more, ….” No would in the if-clause.","on_screen":"✗ If I would have researched more, I would have found a better project.   ✓ If I had researched more, …","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “I wish I listened to Lina last year.”? … Think! … It should be “I wish I had listened to Lina last year.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about a choice I regret and what I learned.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can talk about a choice I regret and what I learned.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: third conditional, wish / if only / should have, decision collocations, clear modifiers (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع الشرط الثالث وwish وif only وshould have ومتلازمات القرار والمُعدِّلات الواضحة.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: If I would have researched more, I would have found a better project. — الصحيح: If I had researched more, …","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أتحدث عن اختيار أندم عليه وما تعلّمته منه."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"The Volcano That Never Erupted – Adam","body":"Last year, our class had to choose a project for the science fair, and I made a quick decision without considering the other options.\nI chose to build a volcano because it looked easy, but three other groups had the same idea.\nIf I had researched more, I would have found a more original project.\nI wish I had listened to Lina, who suggested a water filter made from sand and charcoal.\nRushing through the experiment, I made the mixture too thick, so the volcano never erupted.\nIf our volcano had worked, we might have won a small prize.\nNow I always weigh the pros and cons before I make an important choice.","word_count":113,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Adam's reflection. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Adam considered all the options before he chose.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Volcano That Never Erupted – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Three other groups also built volcanoes.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Volcano That Never Erupted – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Lina suggested a water filter.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Volcano That Never Erupted – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Adam's volcano erupted perfectly.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Volcano That Never Erupted – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Adam thinks they might have won a prize if the volcano had worked.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Volcano That Never Erupted – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Adam now makes quick decisions without thinking.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Volcano That Never Erupted – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"If Adam ___ more, he would have found a better project.","options":["would research","researched","has researched","had researched"],"answer":"had researched","explanation":"Third conditional.","explanation_ar":"الشرط الثالث."},{"q":"Adam wishes he ___ to Lina.","options":["listened","had listened","would listen","has listened"],"answer":"had listened","explanation":"wish / if only / should have.","explanation_ar":"الندم."},{"q":"Adam made a quick decision without ___ the other options.","options":["to consider","considered","considering","consider"],"answer":"considering","explanation":"Decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."},{"q":"","options":["Rushing through the experiment, Adam made the mixture too thick.","Rushing through the experiment, the thick mixture was made.","Rushing through the experiment, the mixture became too thick.","Rushing through the experiment, the volcano failed."],"answer":"Rushing through the experiment, Adam made the mixture too thick.","explanation":"Clear modifier (no dangling or misplaced modifier).","explanation_ar":"المُعدِّل الواضح."},{"q":"If the volcano had worked, they ___ won a prize.","options":["had","might have","will have","might"],"answer":"might have","explanation":"Third conditional.","explanation_ar":"الشرط الثالث."},{"q":"Now Adam always ___ the pros and cons.","options":["takes","does","weighs","makes"],"answer":"weighs","explanation":"Decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Tell your decision story. Write your notes.","items":[{"q":"The decision: ___","options":[],"answer":"I decided not to go to my cousin's graduation because I wanted to play in a tournament.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses third conditional, wish / if only / should have, decision collocations, clear modifiers (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What happened: ___","options":[],"answer":"We lost the first match, and I missed a special family day.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses third conditional, wish / if only / should have, decision collocations, clear modifiers (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A third conditional sentence: ___","options":[],"answer":"If I had gone to the graduation, I would have seen all my relatives.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses third conditional, wish / if only / should have, decision collocations, clear modifiers (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A wish or if only sentence: ___","options":[],"answer":"I wish I had chosen my family that day.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses third conditional, wish / if only / should have, decision collocations, clear modifiers (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What you learned: ___","options":[],"answer":"I learned that family events don't happen again.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses third conditional, wish / if only / should have, decision collocations, clear modifiers (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your reflection.","items":[{"q":"Plan: the decision, the result, two \"if\" sentences, a regret, a should have, the lesson.","options":[],"answer":"joined a game instead of studying; low grade; if I had studied I would have passed; if I had slept I might have concentrated; I wish I had said no; I should have set priorities; school first","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses third conditional, wish / if only / should have, decision collocations, clear modifiers (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your reflection in 7–8 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Last term, I made a bad decision before my history test. My friends invited me to play an online game, and I didn't want to say no. Playing until midnight, I forgot all about my revision. If I had studied, I would have passed easily. If I had slept well, I might have concentrated better. I wish I had said no to my friends. I should have set my priorities. Now I always think it over before I accept an invitation on a school night.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses third conditional, wish / if only / should have, decision collocations, clear modifiers (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: no would after if? past perfect after wish? clear -ing phrases? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"Playing until midnight, my revision was forgotten\" to \"Playing until midnight, I forgot all about my revision\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses third conditional, wish / if only / should have, decision collocations, clear modifiers (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin the Review Wheel","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["A player spins the wheel and lands on a word.","Say what the word means and use it in a sentence with third conditional, wish / if only / should have, decision collocations, clear modifiers (unit review).","Teammates check: meaning (1 point), grammar (1 point), pronunciation (1 point).","Highest total after 6 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"consequence","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"regret","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"decision","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"choice","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"option","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"risk","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"priority","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"hesitate","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"peer pressure","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"impulsive","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"outcome","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"consider","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"wise","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"reckless","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"If we had booked earlier, we ___ cheaper tickets.","options":["would get","had gotten","will get","would have gotten"],"answer":"would have gotten","explanation":"Third conditional.","explanation_ar":"الشرط الثالث."},{"q":"","options":["If I wouldn't have taken the shortcut, I wouldn't have gotten lost.","If I hadn't taken the shortcut, I didn't get lost.","If I hadn't taken the shortcut, I wouldn't have gotten lost.","If I didn't take the shortcut, I wouldn't have gotten lost."],"answer":"If I hadn't taken the shortcut, I wouldn't have gotten lost.","explanation":"Third conditional.","explanation_ar":"الشرط الثالث."},{"q":"I wish I ___ that expensive jacket. I never wear it.","options":["hadn't bought","wouldn't buy","haven't bought","didn't buy"],"answer":"hadn't bought","explanation":"wish / if only / should have.","explanation_ar":"الندم."},{"q":"You ___ your homework before playing.","options":["should finished","should had finished","should have finished","should have finish"],"answer":"should have finished","explanation":"wish / if only / should have.","explanation_ar":"الندم."},{"q":"He gave in to peer ___ and tried the dangerous stunt.","options":["option","pressure","priority","outcome"],"answer":"pressure","explanation":"Decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."},{"q":"Don't make a ___ decision. Think about it for a day.","options":["hasty","hastily","hasten","haste"],"answer":"hasty","explanation":"Decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."},{"q":"","options":["Standing on the mountain, the whole city appeared.","Standing on the mountain, we could see the whole city.","Standing on the mountain, the whole city was visible.","Standing on the mountain, the city spread below."],"answer":"Standing on the mountain, we could see the whole city.","explanation":"Clear modifier (no dangling or misplaced modifier).","explanation_ar":"المُعدِّل الواضح."},{"q":"","options":["If only I would take a photo of the sunset yesterday!","If only I have taken a photo of the sunset!","If only I had taken a photo of the sunset!","If only I took a photo of the sunset yesterday!"],"answer":"If only I had taken a photo of the sunset!","explanation":"wish / if only / should have.","explanation_ar":"الندم."},{"q":"If she ___ so impulsive, she wouldn't have spent all her savings.","options":["hadn't been","wouldn't be","wasn't","hasn't been"],"answer":"hadn't been","explanation":"Third conditional.","explanation_ar":"الشرط الثالث."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a reflection:","options":["Looking back, the options, I wish I had considered them, I would have chosen.","Looking back, I wish I considered my options, because if I waited I would choose better.","Looking back, my options weren't considered, and if I would have waited, I chose better.","Looking back, I wish I had considered my options, because if I had waited, I would have chosen better."],"answer":"Looking back, I wish I had considered my options, because if I had waited, I would have chosen better.","explanation":"Third conditional.","explanation_ar":"الشرط الثالث."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"A school science fair: Adam's group standing next to a volcano model that didn't erupt, while Lina's sand-and-charcoal water filter attracts the judges; Adam looking thoughtful. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A school science fair: Adam's group standing next to a volcano model that didn't erupt, while Lina's sand-and-charcoal water filter attracts the judges; Adam looking thoughtful"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Choices and Consequences”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Choices and Consequences”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L07-U4-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin the Review Wheel”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin the Review Wheel"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS5-T1","script":"Last year, our class had to choose a project for the science fair, and I made a quick decision without considering the other options. I chose to build a volcano because it looked easy, but three other groups had the same idea. If I had researched more, I would have found a more original project. I wish I had listened to Lina, who suggested a water filter made from sand and charcoal. Rushing through the experiment, I made the mixture too thick, so the volcano never erupted. If our volcano had worked, we might have won a small prize. Now I always weigh the pros and cons before I make an important choice.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U4-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Choice I Wish I Had Made: Language in Use”. Let’s learn third conditional, wish / if only / should have, decision collocations, clear modifiers (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Decision story circle: in groups of four, each student tells a short story about a choice (real or imaginary). The group responds with one third conditional sentence, one \"I wish…\" sentence and one \"He should have…\" sentence. Choose the best story to share with the class. Today you use all of Unit 4: the third conditional, wish / if only + past perfect, should have, decision collocations and clear modifiers. A reflection tells what happened, how it could have been different (third conditional), how you feel about it (wish / if only), what you should have done and what you learned. Here are some examples. If I had asked for help, I wouldn't have wasted so much time. I wish I had chosen a different topic. If only we had started earlier! Be careful! Some learners say: “If I would have researched more, I would have found a better project.” That’s not right. We say: “If I had researched more, ….” No would in the if-clause. Quick check: what is wrong with “I wish I listened to Lina last year.”? … Think! … It should be “I wish I had listened to Lina last year.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about a choice I regret and what I learned.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"If I had checked the weather, I ___ my umbrella.","options":["would have taken","had taken","will take","would take"],"answer":"would have taken","explanation":"result → would have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الجواب ← would have."},{"q":"If Noura ___ her bike more carefully, she wouldn't have fallen.","options":["would have ridden","rode","has ridden","had ridden"],"answer":"had ridden","explanation":"if-clause → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط ← had + التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"","options":["If we wouldn't have stopped for lunch, we wouldn't have seen the falcons.","If we hadn't stopped for lunch, we didn't see the falcons.","If we hadn't stopped for lunch, we wouldn't have seen the falcons.","If we didn't stop for lunch, we wouldn't have seen the falcons."],"answer":"If we hadn't stopped for lunch, we wouldn't have seen the falcons.","explanation":"Negatives: hadn't / wouldn't have.","explanation_ar":"النفي."},{"q":"If you had joined the team, you ___ have enjoyed it. I'm not sure.","options":["might","did","had","will"],"answer":"might","explanation":"could have / might have.","explanation_ar":"could have وmight have."},{"q":"\"If the shop had been open, I would have bought a gift.\" Was the shop open?","options":["We don't know.","It is open now.","Yes.","No."],"answer":"No.","explanation":"The third conditional means the opposite of what happened.","explanation_ar":"المعنى عكس ما حدث."},{"q":"","options":["I would have called you if I would have known your number.","I would have called you if I had known your number.","I would have called you, if I had known your number.","I would call you if I had known your number yesterday."],"answer":"I would have called you if I had known your number.","explanation":"Comma after the if-clause when it comes first; no would after if.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة ولا would بعد if."},{"q":"My little brother broke my headphones. I wish I ___ them on the sofa.","options":["haven't left","didn't leave","hadn't left","wouldn't leave"],"answer":"hadn't left","explanation":"wish + had + past participle for past regrets.","explanation_ar":"wish للندم على الماضي."},{"q":"If only I ___ to the doctor sooner!","options":["went","would go","had gone","have gone"],"answer":"had gone","explanation":"if only + had + past participle (strong regret).","explanation_ar":"if only."},{"q":"I wish I ___ more time to read. (I'm very busy these days.)","options":["would have had","had had","have","had"],"answer":"had","explanation":"wish + past simple for a present wish.","explanation_ar":"أمنية الحاضر."},{"q":"","options":["They should had warned us about the storm.","They should have warn us about the storm.","They should have warned us about the storm.","They should warned us about the storm."],"answer":"They should have warned us about the storm.","explanation":"should have / shouldn't have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"should have."},{"q":"Which sentence expresses a regret about the past?","options":["I wish I lived by the sea.","I wish I hadn't skipped breakfast.","I wish it were Friday.","I wish I could fly."],"answer":"I wish I hadn't skipped breakfast.","explanation":"Past regret or present wish?","explanation_ar":"الماضي أم الحاضر؟"},{"q":"It took us three hours to ___ a decision.","options":["get on","take on","do","reach"],"answer":"reach","explanation":"Use the right decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."},{"q":"If you cheat, you must ___ the consequences.","options":["accept","make","take on","do"],"answer":"accept","explanation":"Use the right decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."},{"q":"He jumped into the sea without checking the depth. That was ___.","options":["reckless","responsible","hesitant","wise"],"answer":"reckless","explanation":"Adjective for a decision-maker.","explanation_ar":"صفة متخذ القرار."},{"q":"I was sure about the trip, but now I'm having ___ thoughts.","options":["double","second","new","other"],"answer":"second","explanation":"Fixed phrase (change your mind, second thoughts).","explanation_ar":"العبارة الثابتة."},{"q":"Which phrase is a natural English collocation?","options":["do a choice","face with consequences","make a risk","weigh the options"],"answer":"weigh the options","explanation":"Use the right decision collocation.","explanation_ar":"متلازمة القرار."},{"q":"","options":["Walking into the classroom, a new poster caught me.","Walking into the classroom, I noticed a new poster.","Walking into the classroom, the poster was new.","Walking into the classroom, a new poster was noticed."],"answer":"Walking into the classroom, I noticed a new poster.","explanation":"Opening phrase needs the right subject.","explanation_ar":"العبارة الافتتاحية تحتاج الفاعل الصحيح."},{"q":"Lina read 9 of the 10 books on the list. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Lina read almost all the books.","Lina read all almost the books.","Almost Lina read all the books.","Lina almost read all the books."],"answer":"Lina read almost all the books.","explanation":"Put only / almost / just / nearly before the word they limit.","explanation_ar":"مكان only وalmost."},{"q":"","options":["The man in the blue thobe dropped his keys near the mosque.","The man dropped his keys in the blue thobe near the mosque.","The man dropped his keys near the mosque in the blue thobe.","In the blue thobe near the mosque, the keys were dropped."],"answer":"The man in the blue thobe dropped his keys near the mosque.","explanation":"Move the modifier next to the word it describes.","explanation_ar":"انقل المُعدِّل بجوار ما يصفه."},{"q":"Find the sentence with a dangling modifier.","options":["We washed the dishes after dinner.","After eating dinner, we washed the dishes.","After eating dinner, the dishes were washed.","After dinner, we washed the dishes."],"answer":"After eating dinner, the dishes were washed.","explanation":"Opening phrase needs the right subject.","explanation_ar":"العبارة الافتتاحية تحتاج الفاعل الصحيح."},{"q":"How can we fix \"Hungry after school, the fridge was empty.\"?","options":["The fridge, hungry after school, was empty.","Hungry, the fridge after school was empty.","Hungry after school, the empty fridge was found.","Hungry after school, I found that the fridge was empty."],"answer":"Hungry after school, I found that the fridge was empty.","explanation":"Choose the best correction.","explanation_ar":"أفضل تصحيح."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a reflection on a decision:","options":["If I would have weighed the pros and cons, I wouldn't make such a hasty choice.","If I had weighed the pros and cons, I wouldn't have made such a hasty choice.","If I had weighed the pros and cons, I didn't make such a hasty choice.","If I weighed the pros and cons, I wouldn't have made such a hasty choice yesterday."],"answer":"If I had weighed the pros and cons, I wouldn't have made such a hasty choice.","explanation":"result → would have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الجواب ← would have."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"i wish i didn't miss the bus yesterday.\"","options":["I wish I didn't miss the bus yesterday.","I wish I hadn't missed the bus yesterday.","I wish I haven't missed the bus yesterday.","i wish I hadn't missed the bus yesterday."],"answer":"I wish I hadn't missed the bus yesterday.","explanation":"wish + had + past participle for past regrets.","explanation_ar":"wish للندم على الماضي."},{"q":"\"You shouldn't have shared your password.\" What does the speaker think?","options":["Sharing the password was a good idea.","You never shared your password.","Sharing the password was a mistake.","You will share your password tomorrow."],"answer":"Sharing the password was a mistake.","explanation":"should have / shouldn't have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"should have."}],"theme_ar":"الخيارات والعواقب","essential_question_ar":"كيف تشكّل خياراتُنا حياتَنا؟","can_do":"I can talk about imaginary past situations with the third conditional, express regrets with wish, if only and should have, use decision collocations, and fix misplaced and dangling modifiers.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أتحدث عن مواقف ماضية متخيَّلة بالشرط الثالث، وأعبّر عن الندم بـ wish وif only وshould have، وأستخدم متلازمات اتخاذ القرار، وأصحّح المُعدِّلات في غير موضعها والمُعدِّلات المعلّقة."});
